WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.421
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Friday, November sixth.

2
00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:07.259
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:11.903
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.903 --> 00:00:13.427
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.427 --> 00:00:23.030
The joint maritime centre has issued its latest Gulf threat update, confirming severe risk in the Strait of Hormuz and substantial risk in the wider Arabian Gulf.

6
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:30.258
In Saudi Arabia, the Houthis claim a drone strike on Dammam's main airport, while Riyadh cancellations continue.

7
00:00:30.258 --> 00:00:34.137
And European flights again faced bomb-threat diversions overnight.

8
00:00:34.137 --> 00:00:36.617
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:37.662
Gulf shipping.

10
00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:45.871
Confirmed by the Joint Maritime Information Centre in Update one eleven, issued with an information cutoff of Thursday, November fifth, at seven a.m.

11
00:00:45.871 --> 00:00:51.674
Central: the Strait of Hormuz remains assessed severe, and the Arabian Gulf remains assessed substantial.

12
00:00:51.674 --> 00:01:05.480
That note packages six recent attacks, including Wednesday's tanker strike about fifty nautical miles north of Qatar in the Arabian Gulf, still listed with crew status, damage, and environmental impact unconfirmed at the cutoff.

13
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.492
No newer UK Maritime Trade Operations attack warning was issued in this window.

14
00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:15.461
Separately, Iran's Revolutionary Guard claims two more tankers were mined.

15
00:01:15.461 --> 00:01:19.662
That is a claim only, with no matching UKMTO warning.

16
00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:31.616
Trade press also reports a seafarer fatality after a Greek-operated product tanker was struck in the Middle East Gulf; that is reported, and it is not yet confirmed as the same Qatar-area vessel.

17
00:01:31.616 --> 00:01:41.983
Tueri suggests operators with Gulf voyages review routing against the current area assessments, and plan for continued attack risk without treating unmatched claims as confirmed.

18
00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:43.393
Saudi Arabia.

19
00:01:43.393 --> 00:01:49.776
Claim only: Yemen's Houthis say a weaponized drone hit King Fahd International Airport in Dammam, with claimed disruption.

20
00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:55.146
Saudi authorities have not confirmed a hit in reporting we reviewed.

21
00:01:55.146 --> 00:02:04.796
Separately, Saudi officials warn of potential danger around the Yanbu oil hub as Houthi attacks continue; that warning is reported through secondary media, not a new US Mission alert.

22
00:02:04.796 --> 00:02:12.047
The US Mission security alert of November second still stands and is not new this cycle.

23
00:02:12.047 --> 00:02:24.036
At about two forty p.m. local time today, Flightradar twenty-four showed about fifteen percent of Riyadh flights cancelled, with twenty-six cancellations against roughly one hundred seventy-three flights on the board.

24
00:02:24.036 --> 00:02:26.276
Earlier days used different bases, so no day-to-day trend can be drawn.

25
00:02:26.276 --> 00:02:35.173
Tueri suggests travelers keep flexible plans and confirm each flight with the airline before leaving for the airport.

26
00:02:35.173 --> 00:02:36.340
Aviation, Europe.

27
00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:47.765
Reported: a Prague to Rome flight was diverted to Venice this morning after a bomb scare, continuing a multi-day wave of hoax threats that has forced diversions and delays across Europe.

28
00:02:47.765 --> 00:02:50.951
No devices were confirmed in reporting we reviewed.

29
00:02:50.951 --> 00:02:56.302
Tueri suggests passengers allow extra time and follow airline and airport instructions.

30
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:57.787
Operations check.

31
00:02:57.787 --> 00:03:04.392
Borders and health, US: the Ebola attestation rule remains in force for flights to the United States.

32
00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:07.961
No new change found on the CDC attestation page.

33
00:03:07.961 --> 00:03:09.297
No attestation, no boarding.

34
00:03:09.297 --> 00:03:20.000
Borders and health, Nigeria: health declaration and Port Health screening remain in place for arrivals, with twenty-one day follow-up contact for arriving travellers.

35
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:27.998
Self-quarantine guidance from Nigeria's disease centre still applies to returnees and arrivals from countries with ongoing Ebola transmission.

36
00:03:27.998 --> 00:03:33.238
A blanket quarantine for every international arrival is still not confirmed with the authority.

37
00:03:33.238 --> 00:03:43.642
Borders, Belize: Canada's travel advice and Britain's Foreign Office now both describe an active thirty-day state of emergency in parts of Belize City and nearby districts.

38
00:03:43.642 --> 00:03:48.968
The emergency remains in force; do not treat older Foreign Office wording as clearing it.

39
00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:54.418
Borders and health, Ghana: Ebola screening and a health declaration remain in place, already in force.

40
00:03:54.418 --> 00:04:02.123
India: the India Meteorological Department's tropical outlook no longer names the Murasu remnant.

41
00:04:02.123 --> 00:04:06.005
Hazards: Mayon volcano remains at alert level three, reported via Philippine media.

42
00:04:06.005 --> 00:04:13.860
Infrastructure: Russian strikes again caused power outages across several Ukrainian regions, reported by officials via media.

43
00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.016
That's today's brief.

44
00:04:16.016 --> 00:04:17.498
Current as of six a.m.

45
00:04:17.498 --> 00:04:20.259
Central, Friday.

46
00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:22.712
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

47
00:04:22.712 --> 00:04:27.269
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

48
00:04:27.269 --> 00:04:29.696
Check the original source before you act.

49
00:04:29.696 --> 00:04:38.767
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

50
00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.517
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

51
00:04:41.517 --> 00:04:42.621
Thanks for listening.
